+## Supplementary Note 21 | Frozen-weight transfer and component control in Han
+
+### 21.1 Scope, chronology and response reconstruction
+
+This extension evaluates the existing control operation on another public study, using the previously trained Shen predictors. The original proposal contemplated target-side fitting. Before any Han score, the inference-only amendment replaced that proposal with transfer of saved weights and source-derived strengths. No Han training, model selection or target coefficient estimation occurred. The original proposal remains in the archive as superseded history, not as the executed design. The three source predictors are evaluated together, without selecting HeLa after observing its outcome.
+
+### Supplementary Table S44 | Transfer design and evidence status
+
+| Item | Executed analysis |
+|---|---|
+| Source models | All three archived Shen models: HeLa, A549 and 293T |
+| Source predictor contents | Two saved repeat baseline fits and one saved selected rank-one matrix per model |
+| Allowed target input | Single responses, control measurements and pair identities; declared unit adapter |
+| Han model training / target calibration | None / none |
+| Published stage | 91 pairs; one aggregate published phenotype; predictions locked before scoring |
+| Reconstructed stage | 88 pairs; fourteen query endpoints; two measured end repeats; 74 algebraic partner dimensions |
+| Shared controls | Both end repeats use the same plasmid and initial-sample measurements |
+| Chronology | Published scores were available before repeat reconstruction; rule and weights unchanged |
+| Registration | Local protocol, amendment and prediction locks; no external registration |
+| Additional analyses | Common-panel restriction, error budgets and deletion sensitivities are post-scoring diagnostics |
+
+Only the DrugTarget growth-screen runs SRR5258688 (plasmid), SRR5258687 (initial sample), SRR5258686 and SRR5258685 (end repeats) enter this analysis.[43] Eight compressed read files total 21,533,213,518 bytes and pass their source MD5 checks. Compact count arrays preserve the numerical inputs needed for replay. A separately checked counter maps the paired identifiers to the archived 700-by-700 reference matrix.
+
+Constructs require an initial count of at least 50 and positive plasmid count. For an eligible construct $c$ and end repeat $r$, the log enrichment is $\log_2[\max(n_{c,r},1)/n_{c,\mathrm{plasmid}}]$. In each repeat, the median over eligible safe-control pairs is subtracted and the sample standard deviation over those controls is used for scaling. The initial measurement defines coverage rather than the enrichment denominator. Single responses are medians over the two orientations of gene/safe-control constructs. Pair responses are medians over both orientations and require at least three eligible ordered constructs, including at least one in each orientation. These rules produce 207 finite single inputs and 88 evaluable pairs among fourteen query genes. They were applied without filtering on model performance.
+
+The reconstructed control-standardized response is a declared reanalysis, not a claim to reproduce the published pZ values exactly. The published-table stage uses its allowed single-response columns and aggregate double response. All three predictors receive the same permitted target inputs within a stage. Gene overlap, rather than the full size of the Han screen, limits the evaluated transfer panel.
+
+### 21.2 Complete fixed comparisons
+
+For each source model, all six predefined outputs and the additive reference are scored. The partner coefficients are 0.1187445294033161 (HeLa), 0.239195727853394 (A549) and 0.1428380896646037 (293T). The separately calculated source complete-error coefficient is 0.9697514197443782 for HeLa and one for A549 and 293T. None is estimated from Han double outcomes. A positive percentage below denotes lower component-control error than the named comparator. Pooled means combine the two repeat SSEs before forming a ratio; they are not an additional replicate.
