+Same-alpha whole attenuation and component control have the same partner projection; their complete-error difference measures the effect of retaining the endpoint correction. It does not by itself compare against a whole-attenuation coefficient selected for complete error. The independently source-calibrated whole comparator addresses that distinction and is not target-optimal shrinkage. Endpoint preservation and the equality of complete/partner absolute SSE changes hold to numerical precision in the saved arrays; these identities are implementation checks, not independent empirical confirmations.
