+
+HeLa and A549 have positive scored alignment in both repeats; the retained correction can therefore improve on closure. The 293T direction has negative alignment in both repeats, so any positive scaling along that fixed direction increases the observed partner SSE relative to closure. Attenuation reduces its damage without repairing direction. This fixed-sample statement does not estimate a dataset-wide learnability limit, and no target-optimal alpha was fitted or used for prediction.
